Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-04-24
Subject: Preserve TAsmLabel class when generating alternate asm symbols
License: expat

`ncgbas.pas` relabels inline-asm labels through:

  ReLabel(tasmsymbol(tai_label(hp2).l));

That path allows `GenerateAltSymbol` to assign `p.altsymbol` back into
`tai_label.l`. But `GenerateAltSymbol` always created a plain
`tasmsymbol`, even when the original symbol was a `tasmlabel`. The
result is that later assembler output walks a `tai_label` whose `l`
slot no longer contains a real label object, and the translated
compiler trips UBSan when `aggas` calls label-only methods through it.

Keep alternate labels in the label class. For label inputs, generate a
fresh alternate label via the existing label factories and copy over the
symbol binding/type metadata. Non-label symbols still use the generic
`tasmsymbol` alternate path.

--- a/compiler/aasmbase.pas
+++ b/compiler/aasmbase.pas
@@ -849,11 +849,27 @@
 
 
     procedure TAsmLibraryData.GenerateAltSymbol(p:tasmsymbol);
+      var
+        l : tasmlabel;
       begin
         if not assigned(p.altsymbol) then
          begin
-           p.altsymbol:=tasmsymbol.create(p.name+'_'+tostr(nextaltnr),p.defbind,p.typ);
-           symbolsearch.insert(p.altsymbol);
+           if p is tasmlabel then
+            begin
+              if tasmlabel(p).is_addr then
+                getaddrlabel(l)
+              else
+                getlabel(l);
+              l.typ:=p.typ;
+              l.defbind:=p.defbind;
+              l.currbind:=p.currbind;
+              p.altsymbol:=l;
+            end
+           else
+            begin
+              p.altsymbol:=tasmsymbol.create(p.name+'_'+tostr(nextaltnr),p.defbind,p.typ);
+              symbolsearch.insert(p.altsymbol);
+            end;
            { add also the original sym to the usedasmsymbollist,
              that list is used to reset the altsymbol }
            if not p.inusedlist then
